e\'s metrics endpoint. Maybe the service isn\'t configured to expose metrics on the expected port, or the Prometheus scrape configuration is misconfigured. Also, checking the pods for user-service to see if they\'re actually running and if there are any logs that indicate issues would be helpful. The user already checked deployments, but maybe the pods themselves have problems. Let me check the pods for user-service using kubectl get pods -n social-network to see their status and if they\'re ready. If the pods are in a CrashLoopBackOff state, that would explain why the metrics aren\'t up. Alternatively, maybe the service isn\'t properly exposed, so Prometheus can\'t reach it. Or there\'s a network policy blocking the metrics endpoint. Also, checking the logs of the user-service pod could reveal any errors or failures in the application that might be causing it to not report metrics. So the next step should be to check the pods and their logs to get more details on why the metrics aren\'t being collected.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl get pods -n social-network"  \nTo verify the status of the user-service pods, I need to check if they are running and in a healthy state. The deployment shows READY=1/1, but metrics indicate no uptime. This discrepancy suggests potential issues like failed pod initialization, crashing containers, or misconfigured metrics endpoints. Checking pod details will confirm their actual state and identify any immediate failures.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 514, 'prompt_tokens': 2481, 'total_tokens': 2995, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc5d-4b47-7132-8265-24e9d9fd9ce2-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2481,