he metrics still don\'t show any data. The next step is to check the logs of the user-service pod to see if there are any errors or issues causing it to not report metrics. \n\nThe \'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd\' tool can be used to retrieve the logs. The correct command would be \'kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc -n social-network\'. This will provide insights into any runtime errors, configuration issues, or problems with the metrics server. If the logs show that the metrics endpoint is not configured correctly or the service is crashing, that would explain the missing metrics. Alternatively, if there\'s a network issue preventing the metrics from being scraped, that\'s another angle to explore. Checking the logs is crucial to pinpoint the exact cause of the problem.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc -n social-network"  \nThe user-service pod is listed as "Running," but metrics show no uptime. To investigate why the service isn\'t reporting metrics, I need to inspect its logs for runtime errors, configuration issues, or problems with the metrics endpoint. This will help identify if the service is crashing, misconfigured, or failing to expose metrics.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=435, prompt_tokens=3864, total_tokens=4299, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc5d-9e0e-7201-8bbe-8dfedf085114-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3864, 'output_tokens': 435, 'total_tokens': 4299}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='2d766a7f-bacb-4279-8d43-a3cb7f71e0f0')]]
