he metrics still don\'t show any data. The next step is to check the logs of the user-service pod to see if there are any errors or issues causing it to not report metrics. \n\nThe \'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd\' tool can be used to retrieve the logs. The correct command would be \'kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc -n social-network\'. This will provide insights into any runtime errors, configuration issues, or problems with the metrics server. If the logs show that the metrics endpoint is not configured correctly or the service is crashing, that would explain the missing metrics. Alternatively, if there\'s a network issue preventing the metrics from being scraped, that\'s another angle to explore. Checking the logs is crucial to pinpoint the exact cause of the problem.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc -n social-network"  \nThe user-service pod is listed as "Running," but metrics show no uptime. To investigate why the service isn\'t reporting metrics, I need to inspect its logs for runtime errors, configuration issues, or problems with the metrics endpoint. This will help identify if the service is crashing, misconfigured, or failing to expose metrics.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 435, 'prompt_tokens': 3864, 'total_tokens': 4299, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc5d-9e0e-7201-8bbe-8dfedf085114-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3864, 'output_tokens': 435, 'total_tokens': 4299}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='2d766a7f-bacb-4279-8d43-a3cb7f71e0f0'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose why the user-service in their social network application isn\'t reporting metrics, even though the pod is marked as "Running". They\'ve already checked the deployments and pods, and the user-service pod is up. But when they tried to get metrics for the user-service, the result was empty, which is odd.\n\nSo, the next step is to look into the logs of the user-service pod. The previous attempt to get logs failed because the pod name wasn\'t fully specified. Now, they\'ve identified the correct pod name: user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc. The user is using the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd tool to fetch the logs. \n\nBy checking the logs, they can look for any errors or exceptions that might indicate why the service isn\'t functioning as expected. Common issues could be misconfigured environment variables, failed connections to other services, or problems with the metrics server. The logs should provide clues about the service\'s runtime behavior. If there are errors in the logs, that could point to the root cause. If not, they might need to check other aspects like resource limits or network policies. But starting with the logs is the logical next step.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc -n social-network"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9434f853f5346697', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 308, 'prompt_tokens': 4868, 'total_tokens': 5176, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc5d-b29c-71e1-b2c7-2b930d4ab789-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc -n social-network