ob="user-service"}` to check if the service is considered up by Prometheus. If that returns no data, then the issue is either the exporter isn\'t running or the scrape job isn\'t configured correctly. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the metrics are on a different port. The user mentioned the service is mapped to port 9090, so the scrape job might be configured to scrape that port. But if the exporter isn\'t there, nothing will be collected. So the query should check for the presence of metrics from that job. Let\'s proceed with the query `up{job="user-service"}` to see if any instances are up. If there\'s no data, that\'s a clear sign the metrics aren\'t being scraped. Then the next step would be to check the service\'s configuration or the Prometheus scrape jobs.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"query": "up{job=\\"user-service\\"}"}', 'name': 'get_metrics'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-962e017fb644ec85', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 500, 'prompt_tokens': 3325, 'total_tokens': 3825, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc5f-0d6a-7ac0-ba47-6bd8ebceaf3b-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_metrics', 'args': {'query': 'up{job="user-service"}'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-962e017fb644ec85', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3325, 'output_tokens': 500, 'total_tokens': 3825}), ToolMessage(content='("{\'resultType\': \'vector\', \'result\': []}", 12)', id='7b3b7b1a-5da8-4d94-9b4a-a21bc12e87d1', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-962e017fb644ec85'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='65f7d225-4e21-476d-bb3a