ing, but Prometheus isn\'t picking up any metrics. The user-service pod is listed as "user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc" in the namespace. \n\nNow, the next step is to check the logs of the user-service pod to see if there are any errors related to metrics exposure. Since the previous attempt to get logs with "kubectl logs user-service" failed because the pod name was incorrect, using the exact pod name from the list should work. \n\nThe exec_kubectl_cmd_safely tool can be used to retrieve the logs. If the metrics exporter isn\'t running or there are configuration issues, the logs might have relevant error messages. This will help determine if the problem is on the application side (not exporting metrics) or the Prometheus side (misconfigured scrape job).\n\nSo, the correct command would be to get the logs for the specific pod name "user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc" in the social-network namespace. This should provide insights into why metrics aren\'t being collected.\n</think>\n\nexec_kubectl_cmd_safely\n\nThe exec_kubectl_cmd_safely tool will retrieve the logs for the specific user-service pod (`user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc`) to identify any errors or issues preventing metrics from being exposed. This will help determine if the metrics exporter is running, if there are configuration errors, or if the service is failing to start properly. \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc -n social-network"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 393, 'prompt_tokens': 4548, 'total_tokens': 4941, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc60-4eb9-7541-b2e3-00a0cfef8e56-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'inp