_operations and get_traces tools didn\'t return any errors, so the service is probably communicating with others, but not exposing metrics.\n\nSo the root cause is likely that the user-service isn\'t exporting metrics. The solution would involve checking if the metrics exporter is present in the container, verifying the scrape job configuration in Prometheus, and ensuring the exporter is running on the correct port and path. If the exporter is missing, they need to add it to the container image or adjust the deployment configuration to include it.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool\n{"ans": "The user-service is not exposing metrics. The logs confirm the service is running, but no metrics exporter is detected. Metrics are not being scraped by Prometheus, likely due to missing exporter configuration in the container or incorrect Prometheus scrape job settings. To resolve, ensure the user-service includes a metrics exporter (e.g., Prometheus) and verify the scrape job configuration in Prometheus."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 522, 'prompt_tokens': 6605, 'total_tokens': 7127, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc61-034a-7d02-8798-970e5798b780-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6605, 'output_tokens': 522, 'total_tokens': 7127}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='53ff67ae-055b-4b28-b926-697dc64989d3'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with a social network application where the user-service isn\'t showing up in metrics. They\'ve already checked several things: the ser