\'t collect any metrics. \n\nThey might need to check the Dockerfile or the deployment configuration to see if the exporter is included. If it\'s not, they should add it. Alternatively, if the exporter is present but not configured correctly, adjusting the configuration to expose metrics on the right port and path would be necessary. \n\nAlso, checking the Prometheus configuration file to ensure that the scrape job is correctly set up with the right targets, ports, and paths is crucial. If the scrape job is missing or misconfigured, Prometheus won\'t collect the metrics even if the service is exposing them. \n\nIn summary, the root cause is likely the absence of a metrics exporter in the user-service container or a misconfiguration in the Prometheus scrape job. The solution involves either adding the exporter to the container or correcting the scrape job settings to ensure metrics are collected properly.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool\n{"ans": "The user-service is not exposing metrics. The logs confirm the service is running, but no metrics exporter is detected. Metrics are not being scraped by Prometheus, likely due to missing exporter configuration in the container or incorrect Prometheus scrape job settings. To resolve, ensure the user-service includes a metrics exporter (e.g., Prometheus) and verify the scrape job configuration in Prometheus."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 616, 'prompt_tokens': 7033, 'total_tokens': 7649, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc61-65ca-73b2-9797-386faaabebac-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 7033, 'output_tokens': 616, 'total_tokens': 7649}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the avai