e exec_kubectl_cmd_safely tool. They can check the deployment\'s environment variables or config maps to see if the metrics exporter is configured. For example, checking if the container has the necessary environment variables to point to the metrics endpoint. \n\nBut first, the logs are the priority. If the logs show the exporter is running without errors, then the next step is to verify the Prometheus scrape configuration. If the logs have errors, that points to a configuration issue in the container. \n\nSo, the next tool call should be to get the logs of the user-service pod to check for any errors related to the metrics exporter. If the logs are clear, then check the service\'s configuration for the metrics port and path. If all else fails, maybe the metrics aren\'t being exported, and the service needs to be adjusted to include the exporter.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc -n social-network"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ad34cdabc94a78f0', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 592, 'prompt_tokens': 5707, 'total_tokens': 6299, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc60-6193-7300-b90f-b8d1164fc24a-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-2x7rc -n social-network'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ad34cdabc94a78f0', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5707, 'output_tokens': 592, 'total_tokens': 6299}), ToolMessage(content='[2026-Mar-17 15:12:37.351446] <info>: (UserHandler.h:932:GetMachineId) MAC address = 6e:e4:65:f0:12:7d\n[2026-Mar-17 15:12:37.351755] <info>: (UserS