n in Prometheus to ensure it\'s pointing to the correct endpoint.\n\nBut since the user doesn\'t have access to the Prometheus configuration, they might need to check the service\'s deployment or pod specs to see if there\'s a metrics exporter configured. If the exporter is missing, they should add it to the container image or modify the deployment to include it. Alternatively, they could check if the service is using a different metrics endpoint and adjust the scrape job accordingly.\n\nIn any case, the root cause seems to be the absence of a metrics exporter in the user-service. Without that, Prometheus can\'t collect any metrics. The solution would involve ensuring the service exports metrics and that the scrape job is correctly configured to gather them.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool\n{"ans": "The user-service is not exposing metrics. The logs confirm the service is running, but no metrics exporter is detected. Metrics are not being scraped by Prometheus, likely due to missing exporter configuration in the container or incorrect Prometheus scrape job settings. To resolve, ensure the user-service includes a metrics exporter (e.g., Prometheus) and verify the scrape job configuration in Prometheus."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 574, 'prompt_tokens': 6997, 'total_tokens': 7571, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc62-50f8-7771-b712-3c36e0aa316c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6997, 'output_tokens': 574, 'total_tokens': 7571}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='719131da-4abe-4d47-9ec0-7eb2f7bf87d9'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with a social network application that\'s supposed to have a user-service, but they\'re not seeing any metrics for it. They\'ve already checked a bunch of things: the service exists in Grafana, the pods are running, the logs show the service started without errors, and the metrics query returns nothing. \n\nFirst, I need to recall the tools available. There\'s get_metrics, which they used and got an empty result. Then they tried checking the pods and deployments, but the initial kubectl command had an error because the pod name wasn\'t correct. They eventually found the correct pod name and checked the logs, which showed the service started but didn\'t mention metrics.\n\nSo the main issue seems to be that the user-service isn\'t exporting metrics. The logs don\'t show any errors related to metrics, so the problem is likely that the service isn\'t configured to expose metrics at all. Maybe the container doesn\'t include a metrics exporter like Prometheus, or the exporter is misconfigured. \n\nThe user tried using get_metrics with the job name "user-service" and "user-service-metrics," both returning empty. That suggests that Prometheus isn\'t scraping any metrics from the service. The possible reasons are either the service isn\'t exposing metrics on the expected port/path, or the Prometheus scrape job isn\'t set up correctly. \n\nSince the logs don\'t mention any metrics-related issues, the root cause is probably the absence of a metrics exporter in the container. The user-service might not be designed to expose metrics, or the exporter isn\'t included in the Docker image. Alternatively, the exporter might be running but on a different port or path than what\'s configured in Prometheus.\n\nTo resolve this, the user needs to ensure that the user-service includes a metrics exporter. If the exporter isn\'t present, they should add it to the container image or configure the deployment to include it. They should also check the Prometheus scrape job configuration to make sure it\'s targeting the correct endpoint (port and path) for the user-service. \n\nSince the user has already confirmed the service is running and the logs don\'t show errors, the next step is to address the metrics exporter configuration. They might need to update the deployment YAML to include the necessary exporter and adjust the Prometheus scrape job accordingly. \n\nIn the end, the answer should point out that the user-service isn\'t exposing metrics, likely due to missing exporter configuration, and suggest adding the exporter and verifying the scrape job settings.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool\n{"ans": "The user-service is not exposing metrics. The logs confirm the service is running, but no metrics exporter is detected. Metrics are not being scraped by Prometheus, likely due to missing exporter configuration in the container or incorrect Prometheus scrape job settings. To resolve, ensure the user-service includes a metrics exporter (e.g., Prometheus) and verify the scrape job configuration in Prometheus."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 597, 'prompt_tokens': 8103, 'total_tokens': 8700, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc62-6c9f-71f3-9947-a665d8a8db53-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8103, 'output_tokens': 597, 'total_tokens': 8700}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='55a38920-9bed-415a-a220-3019ba99512a')]]
