r, that\'s the root cause. So the answer should point out that the user-service isn\'t exporting metrics, leading to the absence in Prometheus.\n</think>\n\nThe logs indicate the user-service started successfully but do not mention metrics exposure. This confirms the service is running but **not exporting metrics** (e.g., no Prometheus exporter or metrics endpoint configured). The absence of metrics in Prometheus (`get_metrics` returned empty results) confirms the root cause: the service lacks a metrics exporter or the exporter is misconfigured. \n\n**Mitigation**: Ensure the user-service container includes a metrics exporter (e.g., Prometheus) and that the exporter is configured to expose metrics on the correct port/path (e.g., `/metrics`). If the exporter is missing, update the container image or add the exporter to the deployment configuration.\n\nsubmit_tool\n{"ans": "The user-service is not exposing metrics. The logs confirm the service is running, but no metrics exporter is detected. Metrics are not being scraped by Prometheus, likely due to missing exporter configuration in the container or incorrect Prometheus scrape job settings. To resolve, ensure the user-service includes a metrics exporter (e.g., Prometheus) and verify the scrape job configuration in Prometheus."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 541, 'prompt_tokens': 4940, 'total_tokens': 5481, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc60-80ba-7392-948e-3c6fc35566a0-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4940, 'output_tokens': 541, 'total_tokens': 5481}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='45703a22-a1b2-4f7c-