s exporter (e.g., Prometheus) and verify the scrape job configuration in Prometheus."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 485, 'prompt_tokens': 7425, 'total_tokens': 7910, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc62-b0c2-7b31-b33d-43240be04944-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 7425, 'output_tokens': 485, 'total_tokens': 7910}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='76e464a1-5403-464d-b254-eab4fb570fb6'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with a social network application that\'s supposed to have a user-service, but the metrics for that service aren\'t showing up in Prometheus. They\'ve already checked a bunch of things: the service exists in Grafana, the pods are running, the logs don\'t show errors, and the metrics query returns nothing. \n\nHmm, the key issue here is that the user-service isn\'t exposing metrics. The logs confirm the service is running, but there\'s no mention of a metrics exporter. So the problem is likely that the service isn\'t set up to expose metrics, which means Prometheus can\'t scrape them. \n\nThe user tried using get_metrics with the job name "user-service" and "user-service-metrics," but both returned empty results. That makes sense if the service isn\'t exporting metrics. The next step would be to check if the metrics exporter is part of the container image. If the container doesn\'t include an exporter like Prometheus, then there\'s nothing for Prometheus to scrape.\n\nThe user also checked the pods and deployments, and the pod is running. The logs don\'t show any errors related to metrics, so the issue isn\'t with the service crashing or failing to start. The problem is more about the absence of a metrics endpoint. \n\nSo the solution would involve ensuring that the user-service includes a metrics exporter. That could mean adding a Prometheus exporter to the container or configuring the existing service to expose metrics on a specific port. Additionally, the Prometheus scrape job needs to be correctly configured to target the right port and path. \n\nSince the user can\'t modify the container image or the Prometheus configuration directly through the tools provided, the answer should focus on identifying the root cause and suggesting the necessary steps to fix it. The answer should mention that the service isn\'t exporting metrics and that adding an exporter or adjusting the scrape job settings would resolve the issue.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool\n{"ans": "The user-service is not exposing metrics. The logs confirm the service is running, but no metrics exporter is detected. Metrics are not being scraped by Prometheus, likely due to missing exporter configuration in the container or incorrect Prometheus scrape job settings. To resolve, ensure the user-service includes a metrics exporter (e.g., Prometheus) and verify the scrape job configuration in Prometheus."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 477, 'prompt_tokens': 8531, 'total_tokens': 9008, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc62-c83a-7201-8c56-d52fddf923c1-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8531, 'output_tokens': 477, 'total_tokens': 9008}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='b2d075f4-9a3f-4d71-9801-8d84d2203269')]]
