th, and job name).  \n\nSince the user-service pod is running but no metrics are collected, the most likely issue is the absence of a metrics exporter. The next step is to confirm this by checking the container image and configuration.  \n\n**Tool Choice**: `exec_kubectl_cmd_safely`  \n**Reasoning**: This tool allows us to inspect the user-service pod\'s container image and configuration to verify if a metrics exporter is present.  \n\n```json\n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "arguments": {\n    "command": "kubectl describe pod user-service-<pod-name> -n social-network"\n  }\n}\n```  \n\nThis command will reveal the container image and any environment variables or configurations related to metrics exposure. If no exporter is detected, the next step is to update the Prometheus scrape job or integrate a metrics exporter into the container.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=514, prompt_tokens=3240, total_tokens=3754, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc66-d000-7ff2-b496-a057b33e5cc5-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3240, 'output_tokens': 514, 'total_tokens': 3754}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='6422426b-0842-4038-ad15-8f76dc981ebc')]]
